                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Barlow, United
                        States marshal, to Mr. Fish, Secretary of
                        State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">New York</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1869-07-15"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 15,
                        1869</date>.</dateline>
                <p rendition="#flush"><seg type="margin">103]</seg> *<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Secretary of State</hi>:</p>
                <p>Have sent more marines to Gardner’s Island. Troops not needed at present. There
                    will be no trouble in getting the men on Gardner’s Island to disperse, I think.
                    I shall act discreetly and make no commotion.</p>
                <p>The cutters and tugs have done all I asked; but I wish to know that I can depend
                    on them.</p>
                <p>Grinnell has given me every assistance possible, but is away to-day.</p>
                <p>We can find no trace of the William Forster. Perhaps she is to come from some
                    other port to take up men.</p>
                <p>All is quiet, apparently: but we are looking out.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>FRANCIS C. BARLOW.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
